# %% [markdown]
# ### Predicted Y per row
#
# The columns are called `predicted_Y` by default, set by `prediction_col`
# under Advanced settings:
#
# - `predicted_Y`: most likely value
# - `predicted_Y_p`: its probability
# - `predicted_Y_reported`: the value actually in the data
# - `predicted_Y_p_reported`: the probability the model gives the reported value
# - `predicted_Y_role`: target, holdout, development or outside window
# - `predicted_Y_differs`: True when predicted and reported are different
#
# Differences in `development` and `holdout` are in sample and only a
# diagnostic. Use them as a reference for what is normal, and see if
# `target` is higher.

